# /etc/fstab -- the filesystems of the LikeOS live medium
#
# Read by init at start-up, and by mount and umount.  One filesystem per
# line, six fields separated by blanks:
#
#   <file system>  <mount point>  <type>  <options>  <dump>  <pass>
#
# The root (the live medium's ext4 partition) and /ram (the RAM filesystem
# luakit keeps its caches and databases in) are mounted by the kernel and
# need no line here.  Every line that is not marked noauto is mounted at
# start-up, after the filesystems with a pass number above 0 have been
# checked.  See fstab(5).
#
